===Etymology===
From {{proto|Slavic|злато|lang=ru}} (Old Church Slavonic {{term|злато|lang=cu}}), from {{proto|Indo-European|ghəl|lang=ru}}. Cognate with Ukrainian {{term|золото|lang=uk}}, Belarusian {{term|золата|lang=be}}, Bulgarian {{term|злато|lang=bg}}, Serbian {{term|злато|lang=sh|sc=Cyrl}}, Slovenian ''[[zlato]]'', Czech ''[[zlato]]'', Slovakian ''[[zlato]]'', Polish ''[[złoto]]''. The Indo-European root is also the source of Germanic ''*gulþa-'' (English [[gold]]).

